# A fork's middle element is used dyadically; n_ot is monadic, and the
# error points at it.
== SOURCE
[r_ev n_ot t_ally] 1 2
== ERROR
error[type-mismatch]: expected Bool or Int, found Int -> a at 6..10
  note: in the train `[r_ev n_ot t_ally]`, `n_ot` is applied as `(r_ev x) n_ot (t_ally x)`, where x is the train's argument
  note: `n_ot` takes one argument, but here it is given two
